     The ttiimmeerrffdd__ccrreeaattee() system call creates a ttiimmeerrffdd object and returns its
     file descriptor.  If an error occurs, -1 is returned and the global vari‐
     able _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

     The ttiimmeerrffdd__ggeettttiimmee() and ttiimmeerrffdd__sseettttiimmee() system calls return 0 on suc‐
     cess.  If an error occurs, -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o
     is set to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The ttiimmeerrffdd__ccrreeaattee() system call fails if:

     [EINVAL]           The specified _c_l_o_c_k_i_d is not supported.

     [EINVAL]           The provided _f_l_a_g_s are invalid.

     [EMFILE]           The per-process descriptor table is full.

     [ENFILE]           The system file table is full.

     [ENOMEM]           The kernel failed to allocate enough memory for the
                        timer.

     Both ttiimmeerrffdd__ggeettttiimmee() and ttiimmeerrffdd__sseettttiimmee() system calls fail if:

     [EBADF]            The provided _f_d is invalid.

     [EFAULT]           The addresses provided by _c_u_r_r___v_a_l_u_e, _n_e_w___v_a_l_u_e, or
                        _o_l_d___v_a_l_u_e are invalid.

     [EINVAL]           The provided _f_d is valid, but was not generated by
                        ttiimmeerrffdd__ccrreeaattee().

     The following errors only apply to ttiimmeerrffdd__sseettttiimmee():

     [EINVAL]           The provided _f_l_a_g_s are invalid.

     [EINVAL]           A nanosecond field in the _n_e_w___v_a_l_u_e argument specified
                        a value less than zero, or greater than or equal to
                        10^9.

     [ECANCELED]        The timer was created with the clock ID
                        CLOCK_REALTIME, was configured with the
                        TFD_TIMER_CANCEL_ON_SET flag, and the system realtime
                        clock experienced a discontinuous change without being
                        read.

     A read from a ttiimmeerrffdd object fails if:

     [EAGAIN]           The timer's expiration counter is zero and the ttiimmeerrffdd
                        object is set for non-blocking I/O.

     [ECANCELED]        The timer was created with the clock ID
                        CLOCK_REALTIME, was configured with the
                        TFD_TIMER_CANCEL_ON_SET flag, and the system realtime
                        clock experienced a discontinuous change.

     [EINVAL]           The size of the read buffer is not large enough to
                        hold the _u_i_n_t_6_4___t sized timer expiration counter.

